This product includes software and model weights developed by third parties.
Nothing below is vendored in this repository unless stated; the entries say how each
one is used, so a reader can tell "we call it" from "we ship it".

## Runtime dependencies (installed, not vendored)

- **ComfyUI** — https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI — GPL-3.0.
  Used as an external executor. This project talks to it over HTTP through the Comfy
  SDK v2 API; no ComfyUI source is bundled or linked into the application.
- **Comfy SDK** (`comfy-sdk`) and **comfy-api-proxy** — https://github.com/Comfy-Org —
  MIT. Python dependencies installed from PyPI.
- **FastAPI**, **Uvicorn**, **python-multipart**, **Pillow** — their respective
  licences, installed from PyPI.
- **Inter** (typeface) — SIL Open Font License 1.1. Self-hosted subset, see
  `src/static/fonts/LICENSE-Inter.txt`.

## Model weights (downloaded by the user, never shipped here)

- **FLUX 3 Klein** and **FLUX 2 Klein** — Black Forest Labs. Their own licences; the
  character generator's repository is access-gated and needs the user's own account.
- **LTX 2.5** and the **Ripple** IC-LoRA — Lightricks / the Ripple authors.
- **MiniMax H3** and the `h3_character_swap_v1.5` LoRA — MiniMax and akatz-ai.

Exact files, revisions and the licences we can and cannot use commercially are listed
in `docs/model-licences.md`. If a licence there and this file disagree, the model
licence wins.

## Node packs (installed into the user's ComfyUI)

The packs declared in `dependencies.json` are cloned or installed from the Comfy
registry by `make deps`. They remain the property of their authors and keep their own
licences; this project neither relicenses nor redistributes them.

